            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Kannada for mother's elder sister, then the Kannada for a nephew."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಭಾವ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಭಾವ — bhāva — \"a brother-in-law\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ನನ್ನ ಅಕ್ಕನ ಗಂಡ, ಅಂದರೆ ನನ್ನ ಭಾವ, ವೈದ್ಯರು. nanna akkana gaṇḍa, andare nanna bhāva, vaidyaru. My elder sister's husband, that is, my brother-in-law, is a doctor."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "An elder sister's husband, or a husband's elder brother."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಭಾವ (bhāva), the kinship word, is usually traced to Sanskrit bhāvuka, \"a sister's husband\" (Monier-Williams). It is a different word from bhāva, \"being, feeling\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
